### Make ConfigModule global with isGlobal

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/configuration.md

Set isGlobal to true in ConfigModule.forRoot() to avoid importing ConfigModule in other modules. Once loaded in the root module, it is available everywhere.

```typescript
ConfigModule.forRoot({
  isGlobal: true,
});
```

--------------------------------

### Import ConfigModule in AppModule

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/configuration.md

Import ConfigModule into the root AppModule using the forRoot() static method. This loads and parses the default .env file and registers ConfigService.

```typescript
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ConfigModule } from '@nestjs/config';

@Module({
  imports: [ConfigModule.forRoot()],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

